  – Drone_4 (≈25.8)
  – Drone_2 (≈30.6)
  – Drone_5 (≈31.1)
  Thus, we chose the four closest – Drone_8, Drone_1, Drone_4, and Drone_2 – to assign to Field_2.

6. The one remaining drone (Drone_5) was then assigned to the field with the next highest threat (Field_1, threat 0.05). Field_3, although needing 2 for full protection, is lower in threat (0.03) and so did not receive any of the remaining drone.

7. The final assignments – while disregarding the drones’ prior states – are as shown above.

This completes the group assignment while ensuring the most threatened field (Field_4) is fully protected, and the remaining drones are distributed in order of field threat and proximity.
